The Bash Shell
Bash is a command shell and language interpreter that is available for operating systems such as Linux, macOS, and even Windows. 
Bash is an acronym for the Bourne-Again shell. A shell is a command-line tool that allows for interactive or non-interactive command execution. 
Having a good background in Bash enables you to quickly create scripts, parse data, and automate different tasks and can be helpful in penetration testing engagements.


